            </profile>
            <profile id="30a0-d421-2200-160b" name="Equipment and options (as printed in WAB2 army list)" publicationId="0641-2ee1-c462-c414" hidden="false" typeId="b19e-ee0c-17d1-6e33" typeName="Equipment and Notes">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="63ac-8f60-d28a-2232">Phalangites: sword, pike, light armour and shield. Persian Archers: sword and composite bows, may have light armour +2 pts each. Experimental Phalanx. Combined Formation. Mixed armour. Counts as a Macedonian Phalanx with these additions: at least half of the unit must be taken as Archers (not enforced). If less than twelve phalangites remain, the unit loses all Phalanx abilities. The Phalangites are always arrayed in the front ranks. The archers in the first rank behind the pikemen may fire at full effect if stationary, other ranks use massed archery. (Alexander the Great p.25)</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
            <profile id="1a8b-c9d1-6771-bf10" name="Armour Save" hidden="false" typeId="0dbe-f4ed-ef08-8e86" typeName="Armour Save">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Save" typeId="603e-2898-6af9-6cf1">5+</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="With conditional bonuses" typeId="5882-dd5a-bc28-4024">-</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Notes" typeId="d5e4-804e-6192-0114">Armour save from armour, shield and barding bonus pips (rulebook pp.95-98); maximum 3+ (2+ for barded cavalry). M already includes encumbrance for armour/barding (p.96). Conditional pips are in the next column.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
              <!-- armour-save -->
            </profile>
          </profiles>
          <infoLinks>
            <infoLink id="66d1-579b-3eff-3187" name="Hand Weapon" hidden="false" targetId="a423-b782-e1ce-43e2" type="profile"/>
