  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="b740-34ff-2409-a643" name="Alexandrian Imperial (Alexander the Great) - List Notes" publicationId="0641-2ee1-c462-c414" hidden="false">
      <description>ALEXANDRIAN IMPERIAL ARMY LIST 331-323 BC (Alexander the Great, pp.24-26). Percentages are by points. Characters up to 25%; the army must have a General (Alexander or a Strategos); it may have an Army Standard Bearer and any number of Hipparchs or Taxiarchs. Cavalry up to 50%. Phalangites at least 25% (at least one phalanx unit). Skirmishers up to 25%. Special Troops, Mercenaries &amp; Allies up to 33%.
Oracles are not used in this army; units may have standards (+5 pts). The list uses the Rise of Macedon list for most troop types. Philip of Macedon, Thessalian Cavalry, Mounted Grooms and Prodromoi are not allowed; League Hoplites, Mercenary Horse and Psiloi are no longer allowed as mercenaries (Polemarch, Greek Psiloi, Greek cavalry and League Hoplites are no longer allowed). Units labelled (EX) are hypothetical. Greek Mercenaries (Greek Mercenaries list; Macedonian characters may join them), Thracians (a Chieftain may command them; no Shamans), Late Achaemenid Persian allies from the End of Persia list (no Kardakes or scythed chariots) and Mountain Indians (a longbow skirmisher unit, a javelin and broadsword infantry unit, a Parapamisidae Cavalry unit and Mountain Indian foot) are allies documented only (no pick list). Not enforced: one Hypaspist unit per two Pezhetairoi, Epigonoi or Experimental Phalanx units; Pezhetairoi may not be taken with Epigonoi; one war machine per phalanx.

ARMY COMPOSITION:
[Alexandrian Imperial]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Cavalry: up to 50%
  Phalangites: at least 25%
  Skirmishers: up to 25%
  Special Troops, Mercenaries &amp; Allies: up to 33%
  ALEXANDRIAN IMPERIAL ARMY LIST 331-323 BC (Alexander the Great, pp.24-26). Percentages are by points. Characters up to 25%; the army must have a General (Alexander or a Strategos); it may have an Army Standard Bearer and any number of Hipparchs or Taxiarchs. Cavalry up to 50%. Phalangites at least 25% (at least one phalanx unit). Skirmishers up to 25%. Special Troops, Mercenaries &amp; Allies up to 33%.
Oracles are not used in this army; units may have standards (+5 pts). The list uses the Rise of Macedon list for most troop types. Philip of Macedon, Thessalian Cavalry, Mounted Grooms and Prodromoi are not allowed; League Hoplites, Mercenary Horse and Psiloi are no longer allowed as mercenaries (Polemarch, Greek Psiloi, Greek cavalry and League Hoplites are no longer allowed). Units labelled (EX) are hypothetical. Greek Mercenaries (Greek Mercenaries list; Macedonian characters may join them), Thracians (a Chieftain may command them; no Shamans), Late Achaemenid Persian allies from the End of Persia list (no Kardakes or scythed chariots) and Mountain Indians (a longbow skirmisher unit, a javelin and broadsword infantry unit, a Parapamisidae Cavalry unit and Mountain Indian foot) are allies documented only (no pick list). Not enforced: one Hypaspist unit per two Pezhetairoi, Epigonoi or Experimental Phalanx units; Pezhetairoi may not be taken with Epigonoi; one war machine per phalanx.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
